There are six ways , through which we can create the ec2 instances:

| Method             | How you create EC2           |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------- |
| **AWS Console**    | Click buttons                |
| **AWS CLI**        | Commands                     |
| **Boto3**(AWS API)   Python code                  |
| **AWS CDK**        | Programming language code    |
| **Terraform**      | Infrastructure configuration |
| **CloudFormation** | YAML/JSON template           |

                                                                **AWS API**:

import boto3

ec2 = boto3.client("ec2", region_name="us-east-1")

response = ec2.run_instances(
    ImageId="ami-xxxxxxxx",
    InstanceType="t2.micro",
    MinCount=1,
    MaxCount=1,
    KeyName="my-key",
    SecurityGroupIds=["sg-xxxxxxxx"],
    SubnetId="subnet-xxxxxxxx"
)

instance_id = response["Instances"][0]["InstanceId"]


                                                            **AWS CLI**
aws configure

aws ec2 run-instances \
    --image-id ami-xxxxxxxx \
    --instance-type t2.micro \
    --count 1 \
    --key-name my-key \
    --security-group-ids sg-xxxxxxxx \
    --subnet-id subnet-xxxxxxxx




print("Instance created:", instance_id)
